            "title": "West End Neighborhood House expands Life Lines to age 25",
            "summary": "West End Neighborhood House has raised the age cap for its Life Lines youth housing program from 23 to 25, effective immediately. The program serves foster care and unaccompanied youth, including LGBTQ+ youth.",
            "body": "West End Neighborhood House announced this week that its Life Lines Program \u2014 which provides intensive case management, housing support, employment assistance, and life skills instruction to current and former foster care youth \u2014 will now serve participants up to age 25, up from the previous cap of 23.\n\nThe expansion was driven by data showing that many participants who aged out of the program at 23 were not yet fully housing-stable. The additional two years allows staff to continue working with young adults through a critical period of transition.\n\nThe program continues to serve unaccompanied youth and those who identify as LGBTQ+. Services include housing navigation, educational and training program enrollment, financial education, mental health services, medication management, and employment placement assistance.\n\nThe Life Lines program is located at 710 N. Lincoln Street, Wilmington, DE 19805. Contact: 302-658-4171.",
            "contentSource": {
              "id": "west-end-neighborhood-house",
              "name": "West End Neighborhood House",
              "type": null,
              "url": "https://westendnh.org/programs/life-lines/"
