            "title": "Ministry of Caring's Emmanuel Dining Room expands to seven days a week",
            "summary": "Emmanuel Dining Room at Ministry of Caring now serves hot meals seven days a week, adding Sunday service for the first time. No ID or registration required.",
            "body": "Ministry of Caring announced this week that Emmanuel Dining Room \u2014 which has served hot meals to Wilmington's hungry for decades \u2014 is expanding to seven-day service, adding Sunday hours beginning June 8, 2026.\n\nThe dining room is located at 115 East 14th Street, Wilmington, DE 19801. Meals are served at no cost, with no identification or registration required. The expanded Sunday service runs from 11:30am to 1pm.\n\nMinistry of Caring's broader network of services in Wilmington includes multiple emergency shelters, transitional housing programs, dental care, mobile medical services, and early childhood education. The Emmanuel Dining Room expansion was made possible by an increase in volunteer capacity and a grant from a private foundation.",
            "contentSource": {
