            "id": "NP-008",
            "communityId": "wilmington-de",
            "title": "Delaware Medicaid expansion covers dental for adults starting October 1",
            "summary": "Delaware will begin covering comprehensive dental care for adult Medicaid enrollees on October 1, 2026 \u2014 a first for the state. This affects an estimated 70,000 Delaware adults currently on Medicaid.",
            "body": "Delaware Governor announced that the state's Medicaid program will begin covering comprehensive dental care for adult enrollees starting October 1, 2026. Previously, adult Medicaid coverage in Delaware was limited to emergency dental extractions only.\n\nThe expansion includes preventive care (cleanings, X-rays), restorative services (fillings, crowns), and oral surgery. Orthodontia and cosmetic procedures are not included.\n\nAn estimated 70,000 Delaware adults currently enrolled in Medicaid will benefit from the change. No action is required by existing enrollees \u2014 coverage activates automatically on October 1.\n\nFor Wilmington residents, Ministry of Caring currently operates a dental clinic that serves low-income patients regardless of insurance status. Starting October 1, Ministry of Caring will be able to bill Medicaid directly for covered services, reducing or eliminating out-of-pocket costs for eligible patients.\n\nResidents who are not currently enrolled in Medicaid but believe they may be eligible can apply through Delaware's ASSIST portal at assist.dhss.delaware.gov.",
            "contentSource": {
              "id": "de-dhss",
              "name": "Delaware Health and Social Services",
              "type": null,
              "url": "https://dhss.delaware.gov"
            },
            "publishDate": "2026-05-28",
            "type": "policy-update",
            "urgency": "standard",
            "tags": [
              "Medicaid",
              "dental",
              "health",
              "low-income",
              "insurance",
              "clinic",
              "patient"
            ],
            "why_it_matters": "Dental care has been one of the most significant unmet health needs for low-income Delawareans. Untreated dental problems lead to missed work, school absences, and serious health complications. This expansion removes a major barrier \u2014 particularly for residents who've relied on Ministry of Caring's clinic for years.",
            "category_tags": [
